## Why This Is Asked

This question probes designing a latency-sensitive, privacy-respecting, explainable inference service with multi-tenant isolation in AWS, plus lifecycle and cost awareness.

## Key Concepts

- PrivateLink, VPC, Private Data Lake, per-tenant isolation
- SageMaker endpoints, Feature Store, Model Registry
- Real-time explainability paths (Clarify/SHAP) with low latency
- Canary rollout, drift detection, monitoring and cost

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example: route to appropriate prod/canary endpoint
function route(tenantId){
  const inCanary = ['tenantA','tenantB'];
  const ep = inCanary.includes(tenantId) ? 'fraud-prod-canary' : 'fraud-prod';
  return ep;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you enforce strict per-tenant data access controls across services?
- How would you validate explainability fidelity at high throughput?
- How would you handle retraining triggers when drift is detected per tenant?

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates understanding of explainability and governance as essential components of production ML workflows, not just model performance.

## Key Concepts
- SageMaker Clarify for feature attributions and bias detection
- Model Registry and Pipelines for full traceability and lineage
- Lightweight dashboards (QuickSight) for non-technical stakeholders
- Drift detection and automated rollback strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// Call SageMaker Clarify for per-inference feature attributions
const explanation = await clarify.explain({
  model: 'sentiment-classifier-v1',
  data: { text: 'This product is amazing!' }
});

// Retrieve bias score
const biasReport = await clarify.getBiasScore({
  model: 'sentiment-classifier-v1',
  dataset: 'production-reviews'
});

// Register model with explanations
await modelRegistry.register({
  modelName: 'sentiment-classifier-v1',
  explanations: explanation,
  biasScore: biasReport
});
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests data residency, tenant isolation, and end-to-end security in real-time inference.

## Key Concepts
- PrivateLink isolation and per-tenant KMS envelopes
- Tenant-scoped Feature Store and de-identification
- Canary rollouts and drift monitoring
- Rollback criteria and latency targets

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo preprocessor: drop PII, hash identifiers
function preprocess(input, tenantId){
  const deid = deidentify(input);
  const keys = kms.getTenantKey(tenantId);
  return envelopeEncrypt(deid, keys);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test per-tenant key rotation without service interruption?
- What metrics would you use to trigger automatic rollbacks?
- How would you handle cross-tenant model version drift detection?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a cost-aware, low-latency multi-model inference with per-language isolation, explainability, and secure data access via PrivateLink. It also probes rollout discipline and drift monitoring in production.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-model SageMaker endpoints with per-language routing
- SageMaker Clarify for real-time feature attributions
- PrivateLink access to private data lake and data residency
- Canary rollouts and drift monitoring for safe production
- Caching for explanations to reduce latency impact

## Code Example
```javascript
// pseudo-CDK snippet outline for endpoint + Clarify integration
const clarifiyConfig = {
  enableExplainability: true,
  caching: true,
};
const endpoint = new sagemaker.CfnEndpoint(this, 'LangEndpoint', {
  // model shard per language
  endpointConfigName: 'LangMultiModelConfig',
  // integration with Clarify
  dataCaptureConfig: clarifiyConfig
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure latency impact when enabling Clarify explanations at 400 rps?
- What strategies ensure clean per-language isolation while keeping a single endpoint footprint?
